  "slug": "discovery-database-1f96",
  "summary": "Four NAR database updates expand structure-linked annotation and programmatic access, spanning CATH/TED domains, MobiDB disorder, and curated mutation data.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is structure-linked annotation resources being expanded and made easier to consume computationally. CATH and TED broaden superfamily number and diversity by integrating PDB and AlphaFold structures, with new homology detection and automated domain assignment. MobiDB adds a refined controlled vocabulary, a versioned REST API, an MCP server, Nextflow workflows and static datasets for machine-actionable disorder knowledge. ThermoMutDB 2.0 pairs semiautomated LLM-plus-rule curation with mutant structural models, adding 1763 thermostability entries with 3D context. The Chemical Probes Portal update, with 26% more curated probes, is a manually curated resource and fits this thread more loosely. The items differ in scope but share emphasis on curation scale and structural or programmatic accessibility.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
}
